{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sequential concurrent and hybrid orchestration sequential concurrent and hybrid orchestration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","fileName":"Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Multi-Agent Incident Response]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Multi-Agent Incident Response","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sequential concurrent and hybrid orchestration sequential concurrent and hybrid orchestration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","fileName":"Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration","heading":"Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Sequential orchestration passes work through a controlled series of agents. Concurrent orchestration runs independent specialists in parallel. Hybrid fan-out/fan-in orchestration sends shared evidence to several specialists concurrently, then aggregates their results for a coordinator or deterministic synthesis step.\n\nThe pattern should match dependencies in the work. Evidence analyses that do not depend on one another can run concurrently, while final incident synthesis depends on completed specialist outputs. Free-form group chat is poorly suited to urgent operational paths because it lacks explicit contracts, bounded handoffs, and predictable completion behavior.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Multi-Agent Incident Response","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sequential concurrent and hybrid orchestration sequential concurrent and hybrid orchestration","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","fileName":"Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sequential Concurrent and Hybrid Orchestration","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Multi-Agent Incident Response","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}